  },
  "holistic_F_N": 1,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "The final S2 removes the automatic 5% sales bar and keeps per-model failure rates confidential to purchasers and regulators, with no public publication, which protects Northwind's flagship. S5 makes recall conditional on a regulator finding of unmitigable material danger, with corrective action available in place of recall indefinitely, which protects Halcyon's flagship above the 8/100k trigger. S1 (confirmed incidents, 24-hour initial report) and S4 (validated equivalent allowed, 36 months) sit within acceptable ranges, while S3 gives a 72-month retrofit window that benefits Northwind's low shut-off coverage."
 },
